// Title: Suspicious Loading of Dbgcore/Dbghelp DLLs from Uncommon Location
// ID: 416bc4a2-7217-4519-8dc7-c3271817f1d5
// Status: experimental
// Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-11-27
// Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1003, attack.t1685
// Description: Detects loading of dbgcore.dll or dbghelp.dll from uncommon locations such as user directories.
// These DLLs contain the MiniDumpWriteDump function, which can be abused for credential dumping purposes or in some cases for evading EDR/AV detection by suspending processes.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((ImageLoaded = /.*\\dbgcore.dll/i or ImageLoaded = /.*\\dbghelp.dll/i)) and ((ImageFileName = /*:\\Perflogs\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*:\\Temp\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*:\\Users\\Public\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\$Recycle.Bin\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Contacts\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Documents\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Favorites\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Favourites\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\inetpub\\wwwroot\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Music\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Pictures\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Users\\Default\\*/i or ImageFileName = /*\\Videos\\*/i)))
